##### send 't' at +16.2 s
Pulsing FW_TRIG0 (GP25) and FW_TRIG1 (GP21): 1000 cycles at 200 us period.
Watch InstrumentPort-40 TRIG0 and TRIG1. FW_TRIG1 runs at half
the rate of FW_TRIG0, so a capture that shows one without the
other has a buffer or port problem rather than a pin problem.
Done.

##### send 'I' at +18.5 s
Beaconing board identity on InstrumentPort-40: E4654C159F171E34
  TRIG1 (ch17) high 50 ms starts a frame; TRIG0 (ch16) then
  clocks 64 bits MSB first, each valid on TRIG1 at the
  rising edge. Trigger the capture on ch17 rising.
  3 frames, 134 ms each.
  No 36 V and no bus needed: U1801 runs from +3.3V_MCU, so
  this reaches the port with the switched domain dark.
Done.

##### send 'k' at +21.0 s
Emitting one line per second for 10 s. Timestamp these at the host and compare.
A 12 MHz crystal off by 1% shows up as 10 ms of drift per
second; the on-chip counter cannot see that error at all.
